# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
# macOS AppleDouble files (created on exFAT/FAT external drives)
._*
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# local assistant workspace
.claude/

# Source project media — 40MB of original camera captures. The web-ready
# derivatives in public/Images/Projects/ are committed; these originals live in
# Google Drive and on the local drive. See project-media/README.md.
/project-media/

# Generated by scripts/seed-sanity.ts — regenerate rather than commit, so it
# can't drift from the taxonomy it's built from.
/scripts/seed.ndjson

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Photography source files. Originals are archived outside the repo; the site
# serves the web-sized crops in public/Images/site/ (also uploaded to Sanity as
# assets), so nothing here is referenced at runtime.
#
# Raw camera formats must never be committed or deployed:
#   • GitHub hard-rejects blobs over 100MB — two of the DNGs are 126MB each,
#     so committing them would fail the push and leave unfixable objects in
#     history.
#   • Nothing references them; the web-sized WebP crops in
#     public/Images/site/ are what the site actually serves.
# Keep the originals backed up outside the repo so crops can be redone.
*.DNG
*.dng
public/Images/Services/*.MP4

# Full-resolution originals (10-17MB each). Regenerate crops from these with
# sharp; keep them backed up outside git.
/public/Images/About Us/
/public/Images/Alarm Systems/
/public/Images/Services/
